	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The paper states that experts excluded variables with “a high percentage of unacceptable missing values (>30%),” rather than using a standard imputation method in the retrieved text, so Other is the best fit. Because of class imbalance, “oversampling was employed to increase the percentage of the minority class by replicating instances from the minority class.” Preprocessing included merging multiple STAR sources, restricting to lung transplants, excluding prior malignancy and loss to follow-up, and removing 173 variables. A 70/30 split on 30,917 cases corresponds to about 21,642 training and 9,275 test/validation cases. No code-release statement was identified.  ￼

